   "daily_driver": 5,
   "sensible_spice": 1,
   "everyday_livability": 3,
   "expert_rank": 5,
   "rationale": "Two finishing-led mechanical watches with pale silver/white dials and overlapping smart-casual registers; German versus Japanese craft is the only real contrast. The SLGH031 alone covers nearly every day, so the 42 mm, 50 m PanoMaticInverse on leather adds a dressier option but little the Grand Seiko cannot already do. No sport or colour energy."
  },
  "PAIR-V": {
   "differentiation": 5,
   "coherence_expert": 4,
   "anchor_strength": 3,
   "tension_point": 4,
   "gap_test": 5,
   "wear_balance": 5,
   "makes_sense_together": 4,
   "beaten_path": 4,
   "daily_driver": 3,
   "sensible_spice": 4,
   "everyday_livability": 4,
   "expert_rank": 2,
   "rationale": "Classic tool-diver plus dress-GMT split: the compact Doxa owns weekends, sport and water, the cream SBGM221 owns office, suits, dinners and travel with a genuinely useful GMT. Removing either opens a clear gap and the morning choice is obvious. Weaknesses: the GMT is splash-resistant only and the orange-handed Doxa is a stretch in the office, so neither is a true wear-anywhere anchor."
  },
  "PAIR-W": {
   "differentiation": 4,
   "coherence_expert": 3,
   "anchor_strength": 5,
